  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of current in a purely inductive circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the inductance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>mH</mi></math> then the equation for the voltage across the inductor, will be"
  },
